@startuml
' House preamble for Google Cloud diagrams (PlantUML stdlib `gcp` = PlantUML-icons-GCP 6.0.0).
' Start a diagram as this file followed by templates/skeleton-gcp.puml; edit only below the marker.
' Rule (STYLE rule 14): use this library only when the sources name Google Cloud; each provider's
' own icons for its own services. Each service needs its own include, below the marker. Proven on 1.2026.8:
'   !include <gcp/Storage/Cloud_Storage>                  Cloud_Storage(alias, "label", "technology")
'   !include <gcp/Data_Analytics/BigQuery>
'   !include <gcp/Data_Analytics/Cloud_Dataflow>
'   !include <gcp/Data_Analytics/Cloud_PubSub>
'   !include <gcp/Data_Analytics/Cloud_Composer>           (managed Airflow)
'   !include <gcp/Data_Analytics/Cloud_Dataproc>
'   !include <gcp/Compute/Cloud_Functions>
'   !include <gcp/Compute/Kubernetes_Engine>               GKE
'   !include <gcp/Compute/Compute_Engine>
'   !include <gcp/Databases/Cloud_SQL>
'   !include <gcp/Networking/Virtual_Private_Cloud>
'   !include <gcp/Security/Key_Management_Service>
' Macro form: Service(alias, "label", "technology"): exactly 3 arguments (2 fail to render).
' The library has no group macros: frames are `rectangle "Google Cloud" as gc <<GcpCloud>> { }`
' and `rectangle "Stage" as s <<GcpStage>> { }`, styled once below. A stated project or region gets
' its own <<GcpStage>> frame titled with what the source says; unstated ones are absent.
' draw.io conventions (reference § GCP and Azure conventions): title option
'   title Architecture: <Domain> > <Pattern>
' labels "Role / Product" ("Log processing" + technology "Dataflow"); zone pastels as
' <<ZoneProcessing>> <<ZoneStorage>> <<ZoneAnalytics>> <<ZoneServing>> <<ZoneOnPrem>> <<ZoneExternal>>
' (meanings INFERRED from template labels); Batch / Streaming = <<LogicalFrame>> (dashed border).
' house-preamble-begin
' Knob LEGEND_FRAME: colour of the thin frame around the legend ("transparent" removes it).
!$LEGEND_FRAME = "#999999"
!theme plain
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam legendBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam legendBorderColor $LEGEND_FRAME
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 80
hide stereotype
<style>
root { FontName "Helvetica"; FontSize 12 }
title { FontSize 16 }
.GcpCloud { LineColor #4285F4; LineThickness 2; FontColor #4285F4; FontStyle bold; HorizontalAlignment left }
.GcpStage { LineColor #9AA0A6; LineStyle 6; LineThickness 2; BackgroundColor #F1F3F4; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneProcessing { BackgroundColor #E1F5FE; LineColor #E1F5FE; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneStorage { BackgroundColor #FFF8E1; LineColor #FFF8E1; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneAnalytics { BackgroundColor #F1F8E9; LineColor #F1F8E9; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneServing { BackgroundColor #F3E5F5; LineColor #F3E5F5; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneOnPrem { BackgroundColor #EFEBE9; LineColor #EFEBE9; HorizontalAlignment left }
.ZoneExternal { BackgroundColor #FFEBEE; LineColor #FFEBEE; HorizontalAlignment left }
.LogicalFrame { LineColor #4284F3; LineStyle 6; LineThickness 2; BackgroundColor transparent; FontColor #4284F3; HorizontalAlignment left }
.NotStated { LineColor #999999; LineStyle 2; FontColor #666666; HorizontalAlignment left }
</style>
!include <gcp/GCPCommon>
' Numbered steps (optional, STYLE rule 16): $step(1) prints a blue badge in a label, an edge label
' or a legend table row. Knob STEP_BADGE: the badge colour.
!$STEP_BADGE = "#1565C0"
!function $step($n)
!return "<back:" + $STEP_BADGE + "><color:#FFFFFF><b> " + $n + " </b></color></back>"
!endfunction
' house-preamble-end
